            <ArticleTitle>A kindred with red cell pyruvate kinase deficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>954-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is described of mild haemolytic anaemia in a female homozygous for pyruvate kinase deficiency, with 20% of normal enzyme activity and with the unexplained associations that she suffers from angina pectoris and that three of her children died in childhood from a muscular dystrophy presumed to be Werdnig-Hoffman disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
